c yogurt containing the same colony counts of L. || The intervention group was instructed to consume a daily dose of 50 g of Kashk with their weight loss diet for 8 weeks. || / Clinical Nutrition ESPEN xxx (xxxx) xxx 7 Please cite this article as: Razmpoosh E et al., Effect of a low energy diet, containing a high protein, probiotic condensed yogurt, on biochemical and anthropometric measurements among women with overweight/obesity: A randomised controlled trial, Clinical Nutrition ESPEN, https:// doi.org/10.1016/j.clnesp.2019.10.001 || / Clinical Nutrition ESPEN xxx (xxxx) xxx2 Please cite this article as: Razmpoosh E et al., Effect of a low energy diet, containing a high protein, probiotic condensed yogurt, on biochemical and anthropometric measurements among women with overweight/obesity: A randomised controlled trial, Clinical Nutrition ESPEN, https:// doi.org/10.1016/j.clnesp.2019.10.001 requirement of every participant.","found that, lifestyle intervention for 6 months in obese elderly adults led to a decrease in weight changes as well as sig- niﬁcant decreases in the measures of WC, FPG, serum TG, SBP and DBP levels (all P < 0.05) [ 36]. || Between-group comparisons revealed that there were signi ﬁcant differences in the mean changes of BMI (P ¼ 0.018), body fat percent ( P ¼ 0.037) and WC ( P ¼ 0.047) after the intervention period, all of which found to be signi ﬁcantly lower in intervention group compared to the control. || Differences with P < 0.05 were considered to be statistically signi ﬁcant. || After the intervention, within-group comparisons showed that the energy, fat and carbohydrate intakes were signi ﬁcantly reduced among both intervention and control groups (all P < 0.01). || Further, the consumption of ﬁber was signiﬁcantly increased in the control group in within-group differences ( P ¼ 0.005). || Results: Between-group comparisons showed that the intervention group signi ﬁcantly decreased triglycerides (P ¼ 0.013) and low density lipoprotein c