PMID:34444671,34444671,"Effects of 60-Day Saccharomyces boulardii and Superoxide Dismutase Supplementation on Body Composition, Hunger Sensation, Pro/Antioxidant Ratio, Inflammation and Hormonal Lipo-Metabolic Biomarkers in Obese Adults: A Double-Blind, Placebo-Controlled Trial.",nutrients-13-02512-v2.pdf,1.000,15,15,nutrients-13-02512-v2.pdf,1.000,15,"Intervention group showed an increase (p < 0.05) of Vitamin D as well. || Patients in intervention and control groups showed a signiﬁcant decrease (p < 0.05) of GLP-1. || Nutrients 2021, 13, 2512 9 of 15 Intervention and placebo groups were contemporarily associated with a signiﬁcant decrease (p < 0.05) of GLP-1 (∆ =-2.39 pmol/L, CI:-3.27;-1.51 and ∆ =-2.05 pmol/L, CI:-2.89;-1.21, respectively). || The intervention group showed a statistically signiﬁcant (p < 0.05) decrease of body weight (∆ =-2.73 kg, CI:-4.72;-0.74), while no signiﬁcant differences were seen in the placebo group between the end of treatment and baseline (T0). || Placebo alone was associated with a statistically signiﬁcant decrease (p < 0.05) of circu- lating levels of ALT (∆ =-3.39 U/L, CI:-5.94;-0.83) and total ghrelin (∆ =-1.28 pg/mL, CI:-2.39;-0.18), while the intervention group showed a statistically signiﬁcant increase (p < 0.05) in Vitamin D circulating levels (∆ = 5.22 ng/mL, CI: 1.56; || Variables Intervention (Mean Values± SD) Placebo (Mean Values± SD) Total (Mean Values± SD) p-Value General characteristics Gender (women/men) 8/4 9/4 17/8 X2 = 0.019 p = 0.891 Age 57.33 ± 8.86 50.31 ± 9.54 53.68 ± 9.71 0.644 Body composition by DXA Free Fat Mass (kg) 51.31 ± 7.60 51.42 ± 8.31 51.37 ± 7.81 0.569 Fat Mass (kg) 44.31 ± 10.05 43.65 ± 9.84 43.96 ± 9.72 0.922 Android fat (%) 51.71 ± 7.28 52.29 ± 7.33 52.01 ± 7.16 0.921 Gynoid fat (%) 45.42 ± 9.99 47.24 ± 8.93 46.36 ± 9.30 0.520 VAT (g) 1838.33 ± 699.33 1 || Interestingly, a clinical study reported a signiﬁcant increase in serum 25-hydroxyvitamin D3 levels with oral supplementation of probiotic Lactobacillus reuteri strain [43]. || Intervention group showed a statistically signiﬁcant ( p < 0.05) decrease of body weight, BMI, fat mass, insulin, HOMA Index and uric acid.","The intervention group showed a statistically signiﬁcant (p < 0.05) decrease of body weight (∆ =-2.73 kg, CI:-4.72;-0.74), while no signiﬁcant differences were seen in the placebo group between the end of treatment and baseline (T0). || Close to statistically signiﬁcant p-values were found for TMAO circulating levels, which were found to be decreased ( p = ns) in the treatment group after 60 days and increased (p = ns) in the placebo group (∆ between groups TMAO =-2.78 µM, p = 0.083). || 9.24) 0.134 * statistically significant at p < 0.05. || Intervention group showed an increase (p < 0.05) of Vitamin D as well. || Patients in intervention and control groups showed a signiﬁcant decrease (p < 0.05) of GLP-1. || Nutrients 2021, 13, 2512 9 of 15 Intervention and placebo groups were contemporarily associated with a signiﬁcant decrease (p < 0.05) of GLP-1 (∆ =-2.39 pmol/L, CI:-3.27;-1.51 and ∆ =-2.05 pmol/L, CI:-2.89;-1.21, respectively). || Placebo alone was associated with a statistically signiﬁcant decrease (p < 0.05) of circu- lating levels of ALT (∆ =-3.39 U/L, CI:-5.94;-0.83) and total ghrelin (∆ =-1.28 pg/mL, CI:-2.39;-0.18), while the intervention group showed a statistically signiﬁcant increase (p < 0.05) in Vitamin D circulating levels (∆ = 5.22 ng/mL, CI: 1.56; || Variables Intervention (Mean Values± SD) Placebo (Mean Values± SD) Total (Mean Values± SD) p-Value General characteristics Gender (women/men) 8/4 9/4 17/8 X2 = 0.019 p = 0.891 Age 57.33 ± 8.86 50.31 ± 9.54 53.68 ± 9.71 0.644 Body composition by DXA Free Fat Mass (kg) 51.31 ± 7.60 51.42 ± 8.31 51.37 ± 7.81 0.569 Fat Mass (kg) 44.31 ± 10.05 43.65 ± 9.84 43.96 ± 9.72 0.922 Android fat (%) 51.71 ± 7.28 52.29 ± 7.33 52.01 ± 7.16 0.921 Gynoid fat (%) 45.42 ± 9.99 47.24 ± 8.93 46.36 ± 9.30 0.520 VAT (g) 1838.33 ± 699.33 1","Intervent