eﬁcial results of probiotics when the interventions were char- acterized by /C21 12 weeks duration, probiotics dose /C21 1010 CFU/day, in capsules, sachets or powder, and without concomitant energy restriction, and the outcome measures included assessment of body adiposity deposits by evaluating body fat mass and waist circumference, instead of body weight and BMI. || The evidence of probiotics effects on body adiposity may improve and be more consistent in future RCTs which include methodological characteristics such as longer duration, higher dose, non-dairy vehicle, non-concurrent energy restriction and use of more accurate measures of body fat deposits (e.g., body fat mass and waist circumference) instead of body weight and BMI. || We observed that only around one-third of the RCTs that evaluated body weight and BMI reported a signiﬁcant decrease in these parameters, while 50% of RCTs that evaluated waist circumference and total fat mass reported a signi ﬁcant reduction in these variables. || Characteristics of the studies Reduction P a Signiﬁcant Non signi ﬁcant Body Weight (kg) Duration of the study (weeks) /C21 12 (n ¼ 18) 9 (50%) 9 (50%) 0.007 <12 (n ¼ 10) 0 (0%) 10 (100%) Dose of probiotics (CFU/day) /C21 1010 (n ¼ 19) 7 (37%) 12 (63%) 0.477 < 1010 (n ¼ 5) 1 (20%) 4 (80%) Vehicle of probiotic Capsule/Powder (n ¼ 15) 7 (47%) 8 (53%) 0.030 Dairy (n ¼ 12) 1 (8%) 11 (92%) Energy restriction Yes (n ¼ 9) 1 (11%) 8 (89%) 0.136 No (n ¼ 18) 7 (39%) 11 (61%) Number of species /C21 2( n ¼ 15) 4 (27%) 11 (73%) || Characteristics of the studies Reduction Pa Signﬁcant Non signi ﬁcant Body Weight (kg) Duration of the study and dose of probiotics <12 weeks and < 1010 CFU/day (n ¼ 3) 0 (0%) 3 (100%) 0.112 <12 weeks and /C21 1010 CFU/day (n ¼ 5) 0 (0%) 5 (100%) /C21 12 weeks and < 1010 CFU/day (n ¼ 2) 1 (50%) 1 (50%) /C21 12 weeks and /C21 1010 CFU/day (n ¼ 14) 7 (50%) 7 (50%) Body Mass index (kg/m 2) Duration of the study and dose of probiotics <12 weeks and < 1010 CFU/day 