PMID:33054635,33054635,"The combined effects of probiotics and restricted calorie diet on the anthropometric indices, eating behavior, and hormone levels of obese women with food addiction","The combined effects of probiotics and restricted calorie diet on the anthropometric indices, eating behavior, and hormone level(科研通-ablesci.com).pdf",0.873,14,14,"The combined effects of probiotics and restricted calorie diet on the anthropometric indices, eating behavior, and hormone level(科研通-ablesci.com).pdf",0.873,14,"Each probiotic supplement contained six species of probiotic bacteria [Lactobacillus acidophi- lus (1.8 × 10 9 CFU/capsule), Biﬁdobacterium bi ﬁdum (1.8 × 109 CFU/capsule), Biﬁdobacterium lactis (1.8 × 109 CFU/capsule), Biﬁdobacterium longum (1.8 × 109 CFU/capsule), Lactobacillus rhamnosus (1 × 109 CFU/ capsule), Lactobacillus reuteri (1 × 109 CFU/capsule), magnesium stearate, and maltodextrin], and the placebo supplement contained starch. || Nevertheless, the reduction of the appetite score was sig- niﬁcantly higher in the probiotic group than in the pla- cebo group ( p < 0.001). || In addition, serum oxytocin levels increased signiﬁ- cantly only in the probiotic group as compared to the baseline ( p < 0.001), and this increment was signi ﬁcant in comparison with the placebo group ( p = 0.02). || Also, the cognitive restriction score signiﬁcantly increased in the probiotic group at the end of the study compared to the baseline ( p < 0.001), whereas no signi ﬁcant change was observed in the pla- cebo group ( p = 0.7). || Moreover, leptin level signi ﬁcantly decreased in the probiotic group compared to the baseline values ( p < 0.001), while probiotics did not cause a greater signiﬁcant reduction in leptin level, compared to the placebo group. || Consistent with our results, some recent meta-analyses conducted on var- ious populations including individuals with obesity, dia- betes mellitus, metabolic syndrome, and non-alcoholic fatty liver disease reported that supplementation with probiotics might have a minor, but signi ﬁcant favorable eﬀect on fat mass and body weight reduction [ 28– 31,51,52]. || Do probiotics, prebiotics and synbiotics aﬀect adiponectin and leptin in adults? || However, the reductions of these scores were signi ﬁ- cantly higher in the probiotic group than in the placebo group ( p < 0.001).","Also, the cognitive restriction score signiﬁcantly increased in the probiotic group at the end of the study compared to the baseline ( p < 0.001), whereas no signi ﬁcant change was observed in the pla- cebo group ( p = 0.7). || In addition, serum oxytocin levels increased signiﬁ- cantly only in the probiotic group as compared to the baseline ( p < 0.001), and this increment was signi ﬁcant in comparison with the placebo group ( p = 0.02). || Moreover, leptin level signi ﬁcantly decreased in the probiotic group compared to the baseline values ( p < 0.001), while probiotics did not cause a greater signiﬁcant reduction in leptin level, compared to the placebo group. || Results: Probiotics administration signi ﬁcantly reduced weight, body mass index (BMI), waist circumference (WC), waist to hip ratio (WHR), bod y fat percentage (BFP), and trunk fat percentage (TFP) compared to the placebo group ( p < 0.001). || Also, no signi ﬁcant within or between-group diﬀerences were seen in terms ofﬁber and protein intake, and no signi ﬁcant changes were observed in physical activity levels between the two groups at the baseline (p = 0.4) and during the study ( p =0 . || Also, a signiﬁ cant improvement was observed in eating behavior in the probiotic group compared to the placebo group ( p < 0.001).Serum levels of oxytocin increased and NPY decreased signiﬁcantly in the probiotic group compared to the placebo group ( p =0 . || Results with P < 0.05 were considered as statisti- cally signi ﬁcant. || There was no signi ﬁcant diﬀerence in leptin changes between the two groups ( p = 0.1).","Results: Probiotics administration signi ﬁ